14	9a36ed1f-c3f4-4329-893e-f14418917920	NuArt Sculpture Park: Exploring the World of Modern Indonesian Sculpture	nuart-sculpture-park-exploring-the-world-of-modern-indonesian-sculpture	NuArt Sculpture Park in Bandung is a unique artistic destination where contemporary sculpture, architecture, and creative landscapes come together in one inspiring environment. Established as a dedicated space for monumental artworks, the park offers visitors the opportunity to explore art beyond traditional museum walls, allowing sculptures to interact naturally with light, space, and the surrounding environment.\r\n\r\nAs visitors walk through the open-air grounds, they encounter a variety of large-scale sculptures that reflect powerful forms, cultural narratives, and modern artistic expression. Each piece invites a different interpretation, encouraging viewers to experience art not only visually but also emotionally and spatially. The park’s thoughtful layout creates a dynamic journey, where every pathway reveals new artistic perspectives and surprising visual encounters.\r\n\r\nInside the gallery spaces, the experience continues with curated exhibitions showcasing smaller sculptures, sketches, and creative processes behind the works. These indoor displays provide deeper insight into the artistic vision and craftsmanship that shape each creation, offering visitors a more intimate connection with the art.\r\n\r\nBeyond exhibitions, NuArt Sculpture Park also serves as a cultural hub, hosting workshops, educational programs, and creative events that foster artistic learning and appreciation. Visiting the park is not simply about viewing sculptures—it is about stepping into a living artistic environment where imagination, craftsmanship, and cultural expression continuously evolve, making each visit both inspiring and memorable.	Explore NuArt Sculpture Park, an inspiring open-air gallery where monumental sculptures, contemporary art, and creative architecture come together to create a t