raftsmanship, and historical displays offer insight into the nation’s heritage.\n\nContinue exploring regional pavilions from West Sumatra, West Kalimantan, Papua, South Sulawesi, and Bali, each highlighting distinctive architecture and traditions. Take a break at Pasar Nusantara for authentic local dishes, and enjoy sweeping views of the archipelago on a scenic cable car ride.	Rasakan kekayaan dan keanekaragaman budaya nusantara di Taman Mini Indonesia Indah (TMII), sebuah destinasi legendaris yang merangkum seluruh pesona Indonesia dalam satu kawasan terpadu.\n\nPerjalanan diawali di Museum Indonesia, tempat Anda dapat mengagumi busana adat, artefak bersejarah, dan kerajinan tangan dari Sabang sampai Merauke. Perjalanan dilanjutkan dengan menjelajahi anjungan-anjungan daerah ikonik seperti Sumatera Barat, Kalimantan Barat, Papua, Sulawesi Selatan, hingga Bali—masing-masing menampilkan arsitektur rumah adat yang megah dan pameran budaya yang autentik.\n\nDi sela perjalanan, kita akan singgah di Pasar Nusantara untuk mencicipi aneka kuliner khas daerah yang menggugah selera. Anda juga akan diajak menaiki Kereta Gantung (Cable Car) untuk menyaksikan pemandangan miniatur kepulauan Indonesia dari ketinggian. Didukung fasilitas shuttle listrik ramah lingkungan, tur budaya ini menjamin kenyamanan Anda menjelajah nusantara dalam satu hari!	["Pakaian kasual yang nyaman dan menyerap keringat", "Sepatu berjalan yang nyaman", "Topi atau payung pelindung panas matahari", "Kamera atau smartphone dengan baterai penuh"]	Discover Indonesia in One Day: Taman Mini Cultural Tour	Jelajah Keberagaman Nusantara: Tur Budaya Lengkap Taman Mini Indonesia Indah	["Bertemu di titik temu TMII dan memulai eksplorasi warisan budaya di Museum Indonesia.", "Menyusuri anjungan rumah adat tradisional dari berbagai kepulauan nusantara.", "Menikmati keindahan lanskap miniatur kepulauan nusantara dari atas Kereta Gantung.", "Mencicipi kuliner lokal autentik di Pasar Nusantara dan berburu cenderamata khas."]
17	34716d92-1a30-4330-8265-182e42e1fc91	Timeless Braga: Coffee, Art & Retro Vibes Walk ☕🎨✨	timeless-braga-coffee-art-retro-vibes-walk-	Braga isn’t just a street; it’s a feeling. Our journey begins the moment your feet touch the iconic andesite stones of Braga City Walk. This isn't your typical shopping tour—it’s a deep dive into the hidden corners that give this area its legendary charm.\r\nHere’s what we’ll dive into:\r\n- Architecture & Heritage: Marvel at the stunning Art Deco facades while I share bite-sized stories of Bandung’s golden era in the 1920s.\r\n- Coffee Hopping: We’ll take a sensory break at an artisanal coffee spot. Whether it’s the nostalgic Kopi Toko Djawa (housed in a former historic bookstore!) or a hidden modern gem, you'll taste the best of local brews.\r\n- Street Art & Galleries: Experience the "open-air gallery" of Braga. We’ll meet local painters showcasing their work on the sidewalks and pop into cozy art spaces often missed by the average tourist.\r\n- Modern Retro Fusion: Explore the unique boutiques inside Braga City Walk that perfectly blend modern Indonesian brands with a classic, vintage atmosphere.\r\n\r\nThis experience is the perfect mix of nostalgia and Bandung’s modern creative energy. You won't just leave with aesthetic photos; you’ll leave with a piece of the city's soul.	Skip the generic malls and step into a time machine! Join me for an immersive stroll through the heart of Bandung’s history, where colonial architecture meets vibrant contemporary art. From the aroma of legendary coffee to the soul of local street galleries, we’ll capture the true essence of "Paris van Java." Grab your camera and your comfiest shoes—let's discover the magic of Braga!	164	4	29	4	25.00	USD	4	10	1	Easy	["1770958452909-717211503.jpg", "1770958452913-771137910.jpg", "1770958452916-464518668.jpg"]	["Pemandu lokal bercerita (storyteller) berlisensi", "Satu cangkir kopi / minuman khas di kedai legendaris Braga", "Lembar panduan sejarah ringkas dan k