19	7fedb658-d95d-44a8-8dc2-7d774a7012e6	Merak Kecil Island: The "Hidden" Pocket-Sized Paradise	merak-kecil-island-the-hidden-pocketsized-paradise	Skip the "pricey flights" to Bali or the long trips to any famous area in Indonesia that you can named it. Hidden behind the busy industrial area of Cilegon is a small peaceful place with white sand and blue water called Merak Kecil Island. \r\n\r\nIt is perhaps Indonesia’s best-kept "budget" secret. For the cost of a single fancy coffee in Jakarta, you can swap the city's dull concrete streets for a day filled with a sea breeze and an island charm. Here's why this small island is making a big impact and consider your weekend plans sorted!"\r\nThe "Backdoor" to Paradise\r\n\r\n​Who says an epic getaway has to be complicated? Sometimes, the journey itself is where the magic begins. Most people only know the Port of Merak as a noisy transit point for massive ferries heading to Sumatra. But, it lies a tiny miraculous place called Merak Kecil Island. It is just 500 meters from the industrial hustle.\r\n\r\n​To get there, you simply hop onto a colorful wooden fishing boat at Pantai Mabak. As the engine hums to life and the shore begins to fade, the vibe shifts instantly. The towering industrial cranes shrink into the distance, replaced by the sparkling, open horizon of the Sunda Strait.\r\n\r\nTiny Island, Big Magic!\r\n\r\n​Merak Kecil might be small enough to wander across in just 15 minutes, but it’s absolutely bursting with soul. It’s a "pocket-sized" paradise that proves the best things really do come in small packages! Here is why this little gem is so special:\r\n​A Tale of Two Shores: Experience the ultimate vibe shift! One side offers a gentle embrace with calm, knee-deep waters perfect for a lazy float. Cross over, and you'll find the wild heart of the island, where rugged coral rocks meet the spray of the sea—a dream come true for your photo gallery.\r\n​The Dance of Giants: There is a spark of pure wonder in drifting through bright turquoise waves while watching massive ships glide silently along the horizon. It’s a beautiful, surreal bridge between nature’s peace and the world’s steady pulse.\r\n​Your Personal Playground: This island is a blank canvas for your best day ever. Whether you’re swinging in a hammock, sharing a picnic on the sun-warmed sand, or snorkeling to find hidden treasures beneath the surface, Merak Kecil simply flows with your mood. ​"A little pro-tip" for your trip: here’s the easiest route!\r\n\r\n​The Legend of the $3 Trip\r\n​In an era of overpriced "luxury travel," Merak Kecil remains the ultimate hero for students and budget seekers. Thanks to the super-affordable Commuter Line (KRL) and Local Train access, it has become a legendary destination for those who want a "backpacking on a shoestring" experience without emptying their wallets.\r\n​You don’t need a private car, an expensive guide, or a massive savings account. All you need is a train ticket, a bit of curiosity, and a few small bills in your pocket.\r\n​Tips to Be a Pro Traveler:\r\n​The Golden Rule: This island lives by a "Leave No Trace" spirit. Because it’s so small, even a tiny bit of litter stands out. Be a legend—bring your trash back to the mainland with you.\r\n​Sunscreen is a Must: The sun reflecting off that white sand is gorgeous but intense. Don’t let a sunburn be your only souvenir!\r\n​The "Early Bird" Strategy: Catch the earliest train from Tanah Abang. Arriving by 10:00 AM is the golden hour sunset, you can snag the best spot before the crowds arrive and feel like you have your own private island for a while.\r\n​The Verdict: Pulau Merak Kecil isn’t about luxury—it’s about the pure joy of a quick escape. It’s proof that you don’t have to travel far to find a place where the air smells like salt and the world finally feels quiet.\r\n​This trip won't just save your weekend—it’ll refresh your soul!	Short escape to Paradise less than 5$: Chipper than your matcha latte  ​💸​​🍵	86	4	6	1	8.00	USD	1	6	1	Easy	["1771864267958-795300104.jpg", "1771864267961-726564423.jpg", "1771864267963-264039421.jpg", "1771864267964-923509131.jpg"]	["Pemandu lokal pendamping perjalanan", "Tiket perahu penyeberangan tradisional pulang-pergi (Pantai Mabak - Pulau Merak Kecil)", "Tiket retribusi kebersihan masuk kawasan pulau", "Dokumentasi foto perjalanan"]	["Tiket transportasi kereta (KRL/KA Lokal) menuju Stasiun Merak", "Sewa peralatan snorkeling / pelampung di lokasi pulau", "Konsumsi makanan dan minuman pribadi"]	Video call via Zoom or texting 	-6.20880000	106.84560000	published	t	f	0.00	0	0	{"languages": ["english", "indonesian"], "planningStyle": "Budget-Focused", "specializations": ["budget", "adventure", "nature"], "planning_services": {"revision_rounds": 3, "follow_up_support_days": 15, "planning_timeline_days": 1, "consultation_duration_minutes": 30}, "consultation_methods": ["phone", "chat", "video_call"], "trip_planner_deliverables": {"interactive_map": true, "itinerary_format": "pdf"}}	[]	[]	Video call via Zoom or texting 	0.00	Easy	\N	\N	1	2026-02-24 03:21:34.838+00	\N	[{"action": "approved", "admin_id": 1, "timestamp": "2026-02-24T03:21:34.838Z", "new_status": "published", "admin_email": "superadmin@locallytrip.com", "previous_status": "pending_review"}]	f	t	f	\N	0	0	\N	2026-02-23 16:31:07.974+00	2026-02-23 16:31:07.974+00	2026-02-24 03:21:34.84+00	Skip the pricey flights to Bali. Hidden just behind the bustling port of Merak is a peaceful pocket-sized paradise with white sand and clear turquoise water called Merak Kecil Island. A short 5-minute traditional boat ride brings you to calm swimmable waters on one side and dramatic coral rock shores on the other.	Tak perlu terbang jauh ke Bali atau merogoh kocek dalam-dalam untuk merasakan ketenangan pulau berpasir putih dan laut biru toska. Tepat di balik hiruk-pikuk pelabuhan Merak, Cilegon, tersembunyi sebuah surga kecil bernama Pulau Merak Kecil.\n\nHanya dengan biaya setara secangkir kopi, Anda bisa menukar padatnya jalanan kota dengan hembusan angin laut Selat Sunda yang menyegarkan. Cukup menaiki perahu nelayan tradisional selama 5 menit dari Pantai Mabak, Anda sudah tiba di pulau mungil yang memesona ini.\n\nDi satu sisi pulau, ombak tenang dan dangkal sangat cocok untuk berenang santai atau mengapung di atas pelampung. Di sisi seberang, gugusan karang eksotis menyambut deburan ombak, menjadi latar foto yang spektakuler. Anda juga bisa menyaksikan siluet kapal feri raksasa melintas di kejauhan. Pilihan tepat untuk refreshing akhir pekan hemat dan penuh keajaiban!	["Pakaian renang / pakaian ganti yang nyaman", "Kacamata hitam, topi, dan tabir surya (sunscreen)", "Kantung plastik ramah lingkungan untuk membawa pulang sampah pribadi (Leave No Trace)"]	Merak Kecil Island: The "Hidden" Pocket-Sized Paradise	Jelajah Pulau Merak Kecil: Surga Tersembunyi Berpasir Putih dan Air Biru di Selat Sunda	["Bertemu di titik kumpul Pantai Mabak dan menaiki perahu motor nelayan menyeberang ke pulau.", "Berenang dan bersantai di tepi pantai pasir putih berair jernih.", "Menjelajahi sisi karang pulau dengan pemandangan kapal-kapal besar di Selat Sunda.", "Berfoto estetik di spot hammock dan ayunan tepi pantai."]
22	d536d64e-201a-48c3-9e6f-5dced78d28f1	Bali Like a Local: Custom Trip Planning by a Bali-Based Expert 🌴	bali-like-a-local-custom-trip-planning-by-a-balibased-expert	Bali is an incredible destination, but planning it properly is more complicated than it looks. Distances can be misleading, traffic changes everything, many online itineraries are unrealistic, and the most promoted places are not always the ones worth visiting.\r\n\r\nI have spent the last 3 years living in Bali and 2 years professionally designing personalized trips across Indonesia. During that time, I have built practical destination knowledge and a trusted local network of drivers, guides, accommodation providers and activity partners.\r\n\r\nI will create a completely personalized Bali itinerary based on your available days, budget, travel style and interests. Whether you are looking for culture, temples, waterfalls, beaches, adventure, local food, nightlife, wellness, romance or hidden places, every part of the route will be designed specifically for you.\r\n\r\nYour travel plan can include:\r\n\r\n• A detailed day-by-day itinerary\r\n• The most efficient route between destinations\r\n• Recommended areas and accommodation options\r\n• Activities and places selected around your interests\r\n• Realistic travel and visiting times\r\n• Transportation recommendations\r\n• Local restaurants, cultural advice and practical tips\r\n• Trusted local recommendations when required\r\n\r\nThis is not a generic itinerary downloaded from the internet. It is a realistic journey designed by someone who lives in Bali, works in Indonesian tourism and understands how to create a smooth, balanced and memorable trip.\r\n\r\nYou will save hours of research, avoid common planning mistakes and arrive in Bali knowing exactly where to go, what to do and how to make the most of every day.	Get a personalized Bali itinerary created by a travel professional with 2 years of experience designing trips across Indonesia and 3 years 