326	157	\N	191	I would recommend Mount Rinjani in Lombok. It’s definitely one of the most beautiful mountains in Indonesia because the scenery is incredible from the beginning until the summit. The view of Segara Anak Lake inside the crater is something you won’t easily find anywhere else. The hike is quite challenging, especially the summit attack with loose sand, but the sunrise view from the top is absolutely worth the effort. My tip is to prepare your stamina and choose a good trekking organizer because the weather can change quickly.	f	0	active	[]	\N	2026-07-14 10:15:09.772+00	2026-07-14 10:15:09.772+00	f	0	f
327	157	\N	18	For a first unforgettable hiking experience, I suggest Mount Bromo in East Java. It may not be the highest mountain, but the landscape is truly magical. Watching the sunrise over the Bromo-Tengger-Semeru area feels like being in another world. The combination of the sea of sand, volcanic scenery, and the view of Mount Semeru in the background is amazing. It’s also more accessible compared to many other mountains, so it’s a great choice for beginners who want to experience Indonesian mountain scenery.	f	0	active	[]	\N	2026-07-14 10:15:43.335+00	2026-07-14 10:15:43.335+00	f	0	f
328	157	\N	19	My recommendation would be Mount Prau in Central Java. It’s a great option if you want beautiful views but don’t have much experience with long hikes. The famous sunrise from Mount Prau shows a stunning panorama of several mountains, including Sindoro and Sumbing. The trail is manageable, but you still get the feeling of a real mountain adventure. I recommend camping overnight because the night sky there is also incredible, especially when the weather is clear.	f	0	active	[]	\N	2026-07-14 10:16:13.201+00	2026-07-14 10:16:13.201+00	f	0	f
