134	2	192	Bangsring Underwater, Banyuwangi, Indonesia : The Day I Swam Beside Gentle Sharks	bangsring-underwater-banyuwangi-indonesia-the-day-i-swam-beside-gentle-sharks	![Image](/images/stories/content/content-1780391844234-849012006.jpg)\n\nHas anyone here visited Bangsring Underwater in Banyuwangi?\n\nI recently spent a morning there, and honestly, it was one of the most memorable marine experiences I've had in East Java.\n\nAt first, I was nervous about entering the shark conservation area. The word shark naturally sounds intimidating. But the moment I stepped onto the floating platform and saw the blacktip reef sharks swimming calmly beneath the clear water, that fear slowly turned into fascination.\n\nSwimming alongside them felt surprisingly peaceful. They moved gracefully through the water, completely uninterested in humans. It reminded me that many sharks are far less dangerous than the movies make them seem.\n\n\n## Why Visit Bangsring Underwater?\n\n### A Conservation Project You Can Experience\n\nWhat makes Bangsring special is that it isn't just a tourist attraction.\n\nThe area was developed by local fishermen who transformed damaged marine ecosystems into a successful conservation project. Today, visitors can enjoy the ocean while also learning about marine protection.\n\nHighlights include:\n\n👉🏻 Swimming with gentle sharks\n👉🏻 Feeding colorful fish\n👉🏻 Snorkeling above coral reefs\n👉🏻 Visiting the floating house (Rumah Apung)\n👉🏻 Boat trips to Tabuhan Island\n\n\n## My Favorite Moment\n\n### Surrounded by Hundreds of Fish\n\nThe most magical part wasn't actually the sharks.\n\nIt was standing in waist-deep water while hundreds of colorful fish gathered around me during feeding time. The water was so clear that every movement beneath the surface felt like watching a living aquarium.\n\nFor a few minutes, I completely forgot about my phone and camera. I simply enjoyed being present in the moment.\n\n\n## Travel Tips for Visiting Bangsring Underwater\n\n### How to Get There\n\n👉🏻 Located in Bangsring Village, Banyuwangi, East Java\n👉🏻 Around 45–60 minutes by car from Banyuwangi city center\n👉🏻 Easily accessible by private vehicle, rental scooter, or online taxi\n\n### Best Time to Visit\n\n👉🏻 April to October for calmer seas and clearer water\n👉🏻 Arrive before 9 AM for fewer crowds and better visibility\n\n### Entrance Fee\n\nPrices may change, but generally:\n\n👉🏻 Entrance ticket: around IDR 10,000–20,000\n👉🏻 Snorkeling equipment rental: around IDR 30,000–50,000\n👉🏻 Boat transfers and shark conservation activities may have additional fees\n\n### Local Etiquette\n\n👉🏻 Do not touch the sharks or coral reefs\n👉🏻 Follow instructions from local guides\n👉🏻 Avoid littering in the conservation area\n👉🏻 Support local businesses and fishermen whenever possible\n\n\n## Discussion\n\n### Have You Ever Swum With Sharks?\n\nWere you excited, nervous, or both?\n\nAnd if you've been to Bangsring Underwater, what was the highlight of your visit the shark conservation area, the snorkeling, or the incredible schools of fish? \n\nI'd love to hear your experience and travel tips for future visitors. 🌊🐠🦈	f	f	f	124	0	1	\N	\N	active	[]	\N	Bangsring Underwater, Banyuwangi, Indonesia : The Day I S...	![Image](/images/stories/content/content-1780391844234-849012006.jpg)\n\nHas anyone here visited Bangsring Underwater in Banyuwangi?\n\nI recently spent a mornin...	bangsringunderwater, banyuwangi, eastjava, indonesia, sharkconvervation, marinetourism, snorkeling, underwaterhouse	\N	2026-06-02 09:23:54.615+00	2026-10-14 05:02:39.393+00	0
