128	14	197	Soaking in the “Hot Snow” of Kawah Putih Tinggi Raja, North Sumatra	soaking-in-the-hot-snow-of-kawah-putih-tinggi-raja-north-sumatra	![Image](/images/stories/content/content-1779885508457-818136524.jpg)\n\n## A Place That Looked Like Winter in the Middle of Sumatra\n\nI still remember how confusing the landscape felt the first time I arrived at Kawah Putih Tinggi Raja.\n\nThe road was surrounded by tropical forest, humid air, and endless palm trees yet suddenly, in the middle of all that green, there were giant white limestone formations covered by steaming hot water.\n\nIt looked like snow.\n\nNot soft snow from winter. But something older, warmer, and alive beneath the earth.\n\nLocals often call it “Salju Panas” or “Hot Snow,” and honestly, that description fits perfectly.\n\nHave any of you been here too?\n\nBecause I still cannot decide whether this place felt peaceful… or surreal.\n\n\n## The Journey Was Part of the Experience\n\n### Long Roads Through Plantations and Villages\n\nI started the trip from Medan early in the morning. The drive toward Simalungun Regency took around 4 to 5 hours depending on traffic and road conditions.\n\nThe closer we got to Tinggi Raja, the narrower the roads became.\n\nWe passed quiet villages, children waving from roadside houses, and endless palm plantations under the heat of North Sumatra’s afternoon sun. Some parts of the road were damaged and bumpy, which made the trip feel longer than expected.\n\nBut somehow, that difficult journey made the destination feel more rewarding.\n\n\n### The First Sight of the White Crater\n\nThe moment I stepped closer to the crater area, steam slowly rose into the air like fog after rain.\n\nWarm water flowed naturally over white limestone terraces, creating shapes that looked frozen in time. The contrast between bright white rocks and turquoise hot water made the entire area feel unreal.\n\nFor a few seconds, nobody around me spoke.\n\nPeople just stared quietly at the landscape.\n\n\n## Soaking in Warm Water Surrounded by Steam\n\n### The Water Felt Relaxing After the Long Trip\n\nSome areas around Kawah Putih Tinggi Raja allow visitors to soak in naturally warm water streams flowing from the crater.\n\nAfter hours on the road, dipping my feet into the warm mineral water felt incredibly calming. The temperature was not too hot, just enough to relax tired muscles while steam drifted slowly around the rocks.\n\nI sat there longer than planned, listening to the sound of flowing water mixed with distant voices from other travelers.\n\nThere was no fancy facility. No modern resort atmosphere.\n\nJust nature doing everything on its own.\n\n### The Smell of Sulfur Was Strong\n\nLike many volcanic areas, the sulfur smell here can be quite noticeable, especially near the main crater flow.\n\nSome visitors loved the raw natural atmosphere. Others found it overwhelming after a while.\n\nPersonally, I think the smell became part of the memory.\n\nIt reminded me that this beautiful place was still connected to something powerful beneath the earth.\n\n\n## Small Moments I Still Think About\n\n### Conversations with Local Visitors\n\nOne thing I loved most was how local the atmosphere felt.\n\nMost visitors I met were Indonesian travelers, families, and groups of friends simply enjoying the warm water together. Some brought snacks, coffee, and sat near the river for hours.\n\nAn older local man told me that years ago, the road access was much harder than today.\n\n“Dulu orang datang ke sini benar-benar karena penasaran,” he said.\n\nBack then, people came here purely because of curiosity.\n\nAnd honestly, I understand why.\n\nKawah Putih Tinggi Raja does not feel like a polished tourist attraction. It feels like discovering a hidden place people almost forgot to talk about.\n\n\n## Travel Tips for Visiting Kawah Putih Tinggi Raja\n\n### Best Time to Visit\n\n### Visit During Dry Season\n\nThe best months are usually between May and September to avoid muddy roads and heavy rain.\n\n### Come in the Morning\n\nMorning visits feel cooler and less crowded, especially on weekends and holidays.\n\n\n## Entrance Fee and Costs\n\n###Estimated Expenses\n\n👉🏻 Entrance ticket: around IDR 10,000–20,000\n\n👉🏻 Parking fee: around IDR 5,000–10,000\n\n👉🏻 Local guide (optional): varies depending on group size\n\nPrices may change depending on local management and season.\n\n\n## Transportation\n\n### Best Way to Reach the Area\n\n👉🏻 Private car or motorbike is highly recommended\n\n👉🏻 Public transportation access is limited\n\n👉🏻 Some road sections near the destination can be rough and slippery after rain\n\nIf possible, avoid traveling at night because several roads have minimal lighting.\n\n\n## Things to Bring\n\n### Essentials\n\n👉🏻 Sandals with good grip\n\n👉🏻 Extra clothes\n\n👉🏻 Drinking water\n\n👉🏻 Small towel\n\n👉🏻 Waterproof bag for gadgets\n\nThe ground near the hot water area can be slippery because of mineral deposits.\n\n\n## Respect Local Nature and Culture\n\nKawah Putih Tinggi Raja is located near local communities that deeply respect the surrounding natural environment.\n\nVisitors should:\n\n👉🏻 Avoid littering\n\n👉🏻 Respect quiet surroundings\n\n👉🏻 Stay careful around hot water areas\n\n👉🏻 Avoid damaging limestone formations\n\nSome parts of the crater are still naturally active, so following local safety instructions is important.\n\n\n## I’m Curious About Your Experience Too\n\nDid anyone else feel strangely emotional visiting this place?\n\nNot because it was luxurious or famous, but because it felt untouched and honest.\n\nI rarely find places that still feel this raw and natural.\n\nIf you have visited Kawah Putih Tinggi Raja too, I’d love to hear:\n\n👉🏻 Did you soak in the hot water?\n\n👉🏻 How was the road condition when you visited?\n\n👉🏻 Did the place meet your expectations?\n\n👉🏻 And would you go back again?	f	f	f	121	1	0	2026-05-28 12:24:24.538+00	28	active	[]	6	Soaking in the “Hot Snow” of Kawah Putih Tinggi Raja, Nor...	![Image](/images/stories/content/content-1779885508457-818136524.jpg)\n\n## A Place That Looked Like Winter in the Middle of Sumatra\n\nI still remember how conf...	kawahputihtinggiraja, northsumatra, hotspringindonesia, traveldiscussion, hiddennatureindonesia, simalunguntorism, whitecraterindonesia, jungleroadtrip, naturalhotwater, sumatratravel	\N	2026-05-27 12:40:00.167+00	2026-10-15 03:48:07.255+00	0
