54	8	19	Is Temple of Leah Worth Visiting in Cebu?	is-temple-of-leah-worth-visiting-in-cebu	![Image](/images/stories/content/content-1773306243777-611800589.jpg)\n\nDuring my trip to Cebu, I came across a place that many people call the “Taj Mahal of Cebu”, the Temple of Leah.\n\nLocated in the mountains of Busay, this massive Roman-inspired temple was built as a symbol of love and devotion. From the moment you arrive, the architecture immediately stands out with its grand columns, statues, and sweeping views over Cebu City.\n\n\n## What Makes Temple of Leah Special?\n\nThe temple was built by Teodorico Adarna in honor of his late wife, Leah Albino Adarna.\n\nInside the structure, you’ll find:\n\n• Large Roman style pillars\n\n• Statues and sculptures\n\n• A grand staircase\n\n• Panoramic views of Cebu City\n\nThe place feels both like a monument of love and a scenic viewpoint above the city.\n\n### A Popular Stop Near Busay\n\nTemple of Leah is often combined with other Busay attractions like:\n\n• Sirao Flower Garden\n\n• Tops Lookout\n\n• Mountain cafés overlooking Cebu\n\nIt’s an easy stop if you're exploring the highlands of Cebu.\n\n\n## Discussion\n\nFor those who have visited Temple of Leah, I’m curious:\n\n• Did the place meet your expectations?\n\n• Is it worth the entrance fee?\n\n• What’s the best time of day to visit for photos or views?\n\nWould love to hear your experiences or tips for visiting!	f	f	f	113	5	0	2026-04-25 13:34:03.254+00	18	active	[]	12	Is Temple of Leah Worth Visiting in Cebu?	![Image](/images/stories/content/content-1773306243777-611800589.jpg)\n\nDuring my trip to Cebu, I came across a place that many people call the “Taj Mahal of ...	templeofleah, cebuphilippines, cebutravel, culturallandmark, viewpoints, philippinestravel, cebuattractions	\N	2026-03-12 09:05:05.986+00	2026-10-15 06:00:41.322+00	0
