58	8	22	Is Wat Phra That Doi Suthep the Most Iconic Temple in Chiang Mai?	is-wat-phra-that-doi-suthep-the-most-iconic-temple-in-chiang-mai	![Image](/images/stories/content/content-1773639333342-561205235.jpg)\n\n## First Impressions of the Temple\n\nDuring my time in Chiang Mai, one place that everyone kept recommending was Wat Phra That Doi Suthep.\n\nThe temple sits high on Doi Suthep Mountain, overlooking the entire city. Just getting there already feels like part of the adventure, with a winding road through the forest before finally reaching the temple entrance.\n\nThen comes the famous 306-step staircase, guarded by long golden naga statues on both sides.\n\nClimbing those steps felt like slowly entering one of Chiang Mai’s most sacred places.\n\n\n## The Golden Stupa and City Views\n\nAt the top, the first thing that immediately caught my attention was the golden chedi (stupa) shining in the sunlight.\n\nThe temple courtyard felt peaceful despite the number of visitors walking around. Bells were ringing softly, incense smoke drifted through the air, and monks quietly moved through the temple grounds.\n\nOne of my favorite moments was stepping to the viewpoint area where you can see Chiang Mai city stretching far below.\n\nIt’s the kind of view that makes you pause for a while.\n\n\n## Is It Worth Visiting?\n\nWat Phra That Doi Suthep is often called the most important temple in Chiang Mai, and I can understand why.\n\nIt combines spiritual atmosphere, beautiful architecture, and one of the best viewpoints in the city.\n\nBut I’m curious about other travelers' experiences.\n\n\n### A Few Questions for You\n\n• Did you climb the 306 steps or take the cable car?\n\n• Did you visit during sunset or daytime?\n\n• Do you think Doi Suthep is the best temple in Chiang Mai, or are there other temples you liked more?\n\nWould love to hear your experiences and tips!	f	f	f	105	1	0	2026-03-18 03:05:00.803+00	19	active	[]	12	Is Wat Phra That Doi Suthep the Most Iconic Temp