67	3	18	Budget Culinary at Cimory Riverside Bogor: Worth the Price or Not?	budget-culinary-at-cimory-riverside-bogor-worth-the-price-or-not	![Image](/images/stories/content/content-1774593501952-686923409.jpg)\n\n## Quick Overview\n\nI recently visited Cimory Riverside in Bogor, mainly curious about one thing can you actually enjoy it on a budget?\n\nThe place is beautiful, sitting right next to the river with a cool, refreshing atmosphere. But when it comes to food, I started wondering if the experience matches the price.\n\n\n## What I Tried (and Paid)\n\n### Food & Drinks\n\nMost of the menu leans toward Western-\n style comfort food pasta, sausages, rice bowls, and their famous dairy products.\n\n• Main dishes: around IDR 50K–100K\n\n• Snacks & desserts: around IDR 25K–50K\n\n• Drinks: around IDR 20K–40K\n\nNot exactly “cheap,” but not overly expensive either for a tourist spot.\n\n### Portion & Taste\n\nPortions are decent, and the taste is pretty consistent nothing too surprising, but enjoyable enough.\n\nFor me, it felt like you’re paying not just for the food, but also for:\n\n• the riverside view\n\n• the cool mountain air\n\n• the overall ambiance\n\n\n## Budget Tips\n\n### How to Save Money Here\n\nIf you’re trying to keep it budget-friendly, here’s what I noticed:\n\n• Share meals (portions are quite filling)\n\n• Skip heavy mains and go for snacks + drinks\n\n• Visit during weekdays to avoid crowds\n\n\n## So… Is It Worth It?\n\nPersonally, I think Cimory Riverside is more about the experience than purely budget eating.\n\nIf you’re expecting super cheap food, this might not be the place.\nBut if you’re okay spending a bit more for the atmosphere, it can still feel worth it.\n\n\n## Let’s Discuss 👀\n\n• Do you think Cimory Riverside is budget-friendly or overpriced?\n\n• What menu would you recommend for someone on a budget?\n\n• Any similar places in Bogor with better value?\n\nCurious to hear your thoughts!	f	f	f	85	0	0	\N	\N	active	[]	17	Budget Culin