145	14	18	Following the Sound of Hidden Water at Curug Cibaliung	following-the-sound-of-hidden-water-at-curug-cibaliung	![Image](/images/stories/content/content-1781324634076-969673277.jpg)\n\n## A Hidden Waterfall Worth the Walk\n\nI recently visited Curug Cibaliung, one of the hidden waterfalls in the Sentul area of Bogor, and honestly, the journey itself became part of the experience.\n\nThe trek wasn't extremely difficult, but it felt like a small adventure. The path led me through forest trails, rocky sections, and streams surrounded by thick greenery. Every step felt like I was moving further away from the city and closer to something untouched.\n\nThen I heard it.\n\nThe sound of rushing water before I could actually see it.\n\nWhen Curug Cibaliung finally appeared between the trees, the first thing that caught my attention wasn't the waterfall itself it was the color of the water. Clear, bluish, and almost unreal.\n\nFor a moment, it didn't feel like I was still near Jakarta.\n\n\n## The Most Memorable Part of the Journey\n\n### The Silence Before Reaching the Waterfall\n\nWhat stayed with me wasn't only the waterfall.\n\nIt was the quiet moments during the trek.\n\nThe sound of leaves moving in the wind.\n\nThe occasional call of birds hidden somewhere in the forest.\n\nThe feeling of crossing small streams while wondering what waited around the next corner.\n\nBy the time I arrived, I felt like I had earned the view.\n\nThe natural pool beneath the waterfall looked inviting, and the water was surprisingly clear. Looking down, I could see rocks beneath the surface almost perfectly.\n\nIt felt like one of those places that still belongs more to nature than to social media.\n\n\n## Travel Information\n\n### Location\n\nCurug Cibaliung is located in the Sentul area, Bogor Regency, West Java, Indonesia.\n\n### Entrance Fee\n\n👉🏻 Approximately IDR 25,000–40,000 per person.\n👉🏻 Prices may vary depending on management policies and parking fees.\n\n### Transportation\n\n**By Private Vehicle**\n\nThe easiest way is by motorcycle or car from Jakarta or Bogor using navigation apps.\n\n**By Public Transportation**\n\nTake a train to Bogor Station and continue with an online ride-hailing service toward the Sentul area.\n\n### Best Time to Visit\n\n👉🏻 Early morning (7:00 AM – 10:00 AM) for cooler weather and fewer visitors.\n👉🏻 Dry season is recommended for safer trekking conditions and clearer water.\n\n### Local Culture & Etiquette\n\n👉🏻 Respect nature by bringing your trash back out.\n👉🏻 Avoid playing loud music.\n👉🏻 Be polite to local residents and guides.\n👉🏻 Follow safety instructions around slippery rocks and swimming areas.\n\n\n## Trekking Tips\n\n### Wear Proper Footwear\n\nSome parts of the trail can become slippery, especially after rain.\n\n### Bring Dry Clothes\n\nIf you're planning to swim, having spare clothes makes the return journey more comfortable.\n\n### Pack Light\n\nThe trek is easier when carrying only essentials such as water, snacks, and a small first-aid kit.\n\n### Check Weather Conditions\n\nHeavy rain can affect trail conditions and water levels.\n\n\n## Let's Discuss\n\n### Have You Been to Curug Cibaliung?\n\nI'm curious about other travelers' experiences.\n\n👉🏻 How difficult did you find the trek?\n👉🏻 Did you swim in the natural pool?\n👉🏻 Which hidden waterfall around Sentul impressed you the most?\n👉🏻 Do you prefer visiting during weekdays or weekends?\n👉🏻 Any tips for first-time visitors?\n\nI'd love to hear your stories, recommendations, and memorable moments from Curug Cibaliung or other hidden waterfalls around Bogor. 🌿💧	f	f	f	178	4	2	2026-06-16 10:24:25.059+00	18	active	[]	1	Following the Sound of Hidden Water at Curug Cibaliung	![Image](/images/stories/content/content-1781324634076-969673277.jpg)\n\n## A Hidden Waterfall Worth the Walk\n\nI recently visited Curug Cibaliung, one of the h...	curugcibaliung, bogorwaterfall, hiddenwaterfallindonesia, trekkingbogor, adventuretravel, natureescape, 