124	4	192	Eating Alone at Pasar Ah Poong Sentul Somehow Felt Surprisingly Comforting	eating-alone-at-pasar-ah-poong-sentul-somehow-felt-surprisingly-comforting	![Image](/images/stories/content/content-1779521596267-375429668.jpg)\n\n## A Slow Afternoon by the River\n\nI arrived at Pasar Ah Poong without expecting much.\n\nAt first, I thought it would only be another crowded food market near Sentul noisy, commercial, and filled with overpriced snacks. But the moment I stepped inside, something immediately felt different.\n\nThe sound of flowing river water replaced the usual city noise.\n\nWooden bridges connected small food stalls above the riverbanks, families laughed softly while eating together, and the smell of grilled satay mixed with fresh mountain air from the surrounding hills. Even though the place was busy, it somehow still felt peaceful.\n\nAnd strangely enough, being alone there did not feel lonely at all.\n\n## The Floating Market Atmosphere That Felt Warm and Relaxing\n\n### More Than Just a Culinary Spot\n\nPasar Ah Poong is located in Sentul, Bogor, and is famous for its floating market concept beside the Cikeas River. The area combines traditional Indonesian food culture with a relaxing riverside atmosphere.\n\nI spent almost an hour simply walking around before deciding what to eat.\n\nEvery corner smelled different.\n\nOne stall served hot soto with fresh lime and chili. Another grilled ikan bakar over charcoal while smoke slowly drifted into the afternoon air. Traditional snacks like klepon, serabi, and tahu gejrot sat beside modern coffee stalls and trendy desserts.\n\nIt felt like Indonesia in one small riverside market.\n\n\n## The Meal I Still Remember\n\n### Eating by the River Alone Felt Surprisingly Peaceful\n\nI finally ordered nasi liwet, chicken satay, and a glass of iced tea before finding a quiet seat near the river.\n\nThe water moved slowly beneath the wooden deck while children fed fish nearby. Occasionally, a cool breeze carried the smell of rain from the distant hills.\n\nI ate slowly.\n\nNot because the food was expensive or luxurious, but because the atmosphere made me want to stay longer.\n\nFor once, I was not rushing anywhere.\n\nAnd honestly, that simple moment became the best part of the trip.\n\n\n## Little Things That Made the Experience Feel Real\n\n### Friendly Vendors and Warm Local Energy\n\nOne thing I genuinely appreciated was how friendly the local vendors were.\n\nA woman selling traditional snacks casually recommended her favorite fried banana stall nearby. Another food seller laughed when I asked for extra sambal and warned me it was “Bogor-level spicy.”\n\nThose small interactions made the place feel human instead of overly commercial.\n\nEven while sitting alone, I never felt out of place.\n\n\n## Why Pasar Ah Poong Works Well for Solo Travelers\n\n### A Comfortable Place to Slow Down\n\nSome destinations feel awkward when visited alone.\n\nPasar Ah Poong was the opposite.\n\nBecause people come here mainly to relax, eat, and enjoy the riverside atmosphere, nobody really pays attention to whether you arrive with friends or by yourself. You can simply walk around, explore food stalls, drink coffee near the river, and enjoy the scenery at your own pace.\n\nIt is not a luxury destination.\n\nBut it feels comforting in a very honest way.\n\n\n## Tips for Visiting Pasar Ah Poong Sentul\n\n### Location\n\nPasar Ah Poong is located in Sentul City, Babakan Madang, Bogor Regency, West Java, Indonesia.\n\n\n## Entrance Ticket & Costs\n\n• Entrance fee: Usually free\n\n• Parking fee: Around IDR 5,000–15,000 depending on vehicle type\n\n• Food prices: Around IDR 15,000–60,000 depending on menu choices\n\nPrices may change during weekends or holiday seasons.\n\n\n## Best Time to Visit\n\n### Morning or Late Afternoon\n\n• Morning visits feel cooler and less crowded\n\n• Late afternoon offers softer sunlight and relaxing riverside vibes\n\n• Weekdays are generally quieter compared to weekends\n\nAvoid arriving too late at night because some food stalls close early.\n\n\n## Transportation Tips\n\n### By Car or Motorcycle\n\nThe easiest way is driving from Jakarta or Bogor toward Sentul City. The roads are relatively accessible and suitable for day trips.\n\n### By Public Transportation\n\nYou can take a train to Bogor Station, then continue using online transportation toward Pasar Ah Poong.\n\n\n## Food Recommendations\n\nSome popular foods visitors usually try include:\n\n• Soto Bogor\n• Nasi liwet\n• Satay and grilled seafood\n• Traditional Indonesian snacks\n• Local coffee and fresh coconut drinks\n\n\n## Local Culture & Etiquette\n\nThe area is family-friendly and relaxed. Visitors are encouraged to:\n\n• Keep the riverside area clean\n\n• Respect food vendors and local workers\n\n• Avoid excessive noise near dining areas\n\n• Bring cash because some smaller stalls may not accept digital payments\n\n\n## A Place I Would Gladly Return To\n\nI came to Pasar Ah Poong expecting only food.\n\nBut somewhere between the river breeze, the smell of grilled satay, and the quiet comfort of eating alone, the place became more memorable than I expected.\n\nSometimes solo travel is not about going far away.\n\nSometimes it is simply about finding one peaceful corner where you can sit quietly, eat slowly, and feel present again for a little while.\n\nHave you ever visited Pasar Ah Poong Sentul alone or with friends?\nWhat food would you recommend trying first there?	f	f	f	107	0	0	\N	\N	active	[]	17	Eating Alone at Pasar Ah Poong Sentul Somehow Felt Surpri...	![Image](/images/stories/content/content-1779521596267-375429668.jpg)\n\n## A Slow Afternoon by the River\n\nI arrived at Pasar Ah Poong without expecting much.\n...	pasarahpoong, sentulculinary, floatingmarketindonesia, solotravelsentul, foodtripbogor, riversideculinary, localfoodindonesia, ahpoongfoodmarket, culinarytravel	\N	2026-05-23 07:34:41.157+00	2026-10-14 23:10:27.513+00	0
