57	2	179	Hiking Volcanoes National Park: Tips Before You Go	hiking-volcanoes-national-park-tips-before-you-go	![Image](/images/stories/content/content-1773546906027-60014761.jpg)\n\nI’ve been researching Volcanoes National Park in Rwanda, and the more I read about it, the more it feels like one of those places that every nature lover should experience at least once.\n\nFrom lush rainforest trails to the chance of seeing mountain gorillas, the park looks absolutely incredible. I’m especially interested in the volcano hiking routes, but I also realized there are quite a few things to prepare before going.\n\nSo I thought it would be helpful to start a discussion here.\n\n\n## What to Know Before Hiking in Volcanoes National Park\n\nFrom what I’ve learned so far, hiking in Volcanoes National Park is not just a casual walk in the forest. The terrain can be steep, muddy, and sometimes unpredictable because of the weather.\n\nA few things that seem important:\n\n👉🏻 Permits are required, especially for gorilla trekking\n\n👉🏻 The trails can be very muddy, even during the dry season\n\n👉🏻 A local guide is mandatory for most hikes\n\n👉🏻 Weather in the mountains can change quickly\n\nIt sounds like preparation really makes a difference here.\n\n\n## Popular Hiking Experiences in the Park\n\nSome hikes that caught my attention include:\n\n### Mount Bisoke Crater Lake Hike\n\nThis trail leads to a beautiful crater lake at the summit, and the views look incredible.\n\n### Mount Karisimbi Trek\n\nOne of the highest volcanoes in the Virunga range, usually done as a two-day trek.\n\n### Gorilla Trekking\n\nNot exactly a traditional hike, but definitely one of the most famous wildlife experiences in the world.\n\n\n## Things I’m Personally Curious About\n\nSince I’m still planning this trip, I’d love to hear from anyone who has been there.\n\n👉🏻 How physically difficult are the hikes?\n\n👉🏻 Is Mount Bisoke manageable for someone with average fitness?\n\n👉🏻 What’s the best time of year to visit?\n\n👉🏻 Any gear that you wish you had brought?\n\nI’d really love to hear your experiences or tips before I finally plan this adventure. 😊	f	f	f	117	0	0	\N	\N	active	[]	28	Hiking Volcanoes National Park: Tips Before You Go	![Image](/images/stories/content/content-1773546906027-60014761.jpg)\n\nI’ve been researching Volcanoes National Park in Rwanda, and the more I read about it, ...	volcanoesnationalpark, rwanda, hiking, gorillatrekking, nationalpark, africatravel, volcanohike	\N	2026-03-15 04:22:59.384+00	2026-10-14 12:58:46.167+00	0
