56	15	180	Training at Dragon’s Lair Gym in Las Vegas, Worth It for Digital Nomads?	training-at-dragons-lair-gym-in-las-vegas-worth-it-for-digital-nomads	![Image](/images/stories/content/content-1773500407030-415066464.jpg)\n\nAs a digital nomad, one thing I always try to keep consistent no matter where I am in the world is my training routine. Work can happen anywhere with WiFi, but finding the right gym in a new city is always a different story.\n\nRecently while staying in Las Vegas, I came across Dragon’s Lair Gym, and it definitely caught my attention.\n\n\n## My First Impression of Dragon’s Lair Gym\n\nThe atmosphere felt very different from most commercial gyms.\n\nDragon’s Lair Gym has this hardcore bodybuilding vibe heavy weights, serious lifters, and a space that feels built for people who really train. Not just casual workouts.\n\nAs someone balancing remote work and training, I actually liked that energy. It felt motivating after spending hours working on my laptop.\n\n\n## Is It Good for Digital Nomads?\n\nOne thing I always consider as a digital nomad is flexibility.\n\n👉🏻 Is it easy to get a short-term pass?\n\n👉🏻 Is the environment welcoming for travelers?\n\n👉🏻 Is it worth the price if you’re only in the city for a few weeks?\n\nDragon’s Lair Gym seems popular among serious lifters, but I’m curious how other travelers or nomads feel about it.\n\n### Curious About Other People’s Experience\n\nFor those who have trained here before:\n\n👉🏻 How was your experience at Dragon’s Lair Gym?\n\n👉🏻 Is it beginner-friendly or mostly for advanced lifters?\n\n👉🏻 Would you recommend it for someone staying in Las Vegas short term?\n\nI’d love to hear your thoughts or recommendations for other gyms in the city too. Always interesting to see how other digital nomads keep their fitness routine while traveling.	f	f	f	108	1	0	2026-03-16 05:42:30.998+00	22	active	[]	41	Training at Dragon’s Lair Gym in Las Vegas, Worth It for ...	![Image](/images/stories/content/content-17