22	15	22	Remote Work at Gardens by the Bay During Sunset — Is It a Good Idea?	remote-work-at-gardens-by-the-bay-during-sunset-is-it-a-good-idea	![Image](/images/stories/content/content-1770622563328-850848666.jpg)\n\nI didn’t plan to work that evening. I just opened my laptop while waiting for the sunset and somehow finished more tasks than expected.\n\nGardens by the Bay during golden hour feels unreal. The sky changes color, the city slows down, and work doesn’t feel as heavy.\n\n\n## Working While Watching the Sun Go Down\n\nAs a digital nomad, I usually work indoors cafés, libraries, coworking spaces.\nBut working outdoors, with Marina Bay in front of me, felt different.\n\nWhat worked for me:\n\n• Open space and fresh air\n\n• Calm energy before night crowds arrive\n\n• Strong mobile data (surprisingly stable)\n\n• A mental reset without fully logging off\n\nIt wasn’t about productivity alone it was about balance.\n\n### Is It Practical or Just Romantic?\n\nLet’s be honest—it’s not a deep-focus setup.\n\nThis spot works best if:\n\n• You’re doing light tasks or emails\n\n• You want creative inspiration\n\n• You don’t need long calls or meetings\n\nFor heavy work, I’d still choose indoor spaces. But for winding down while staying connected? It’s worth it.\n\n\n## Opening the Discussion\n\nNow I’m curious.\n\n• Have you ever worked remotely from outdoor public spaces?\n\n• Would you choose a scenic spot over productivity?\n\n• Any sunset-friendly work spots you’d recommend in Singapore?\n\nLet’s talk. 👇	f	f	f	105	0	0	\N	\N	active	[]	36	Remote Work at Gardens by the Bay During Sunset — Is It a...	![Image](/images/stories/content/content-1770622563328-850848666.jpg)\n\nI didn’t plan to work that evening. I just opened my laptop while waiting for the suns...	DigitalNomad, RemoteWork, GardensbytheBay, Singapore, SunsetWork, WorkLifeBalance, SlowTravel	\N	2026-02-09 07:36:18.539+00	2026-10-14 14:48:26.123+00	0
